From: Yannick Serafini <yannick.serafini@wifx.net>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:52:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Break the MCU/SX130X sync loop out of a poisoned
 reference

ts_updateTimesync() advances its reference sample only under the "done:"
label, downstream of the excessive-drift early return. If the first pair of
a session is itself bad, every later sample is measured against a wrong
reference, looks excessive for that reason alone, and the loop can never
leave the state. Measured on target: up to +24740ppm still at +1918ppm after
57 retries, and a field unit stuck at -900ppm with no natural exit at all.
A poisoned reference shifts txjob->txtime without moving the RF instant, so
downlinks are either silently never triggered or aborted by the TXCHECK_FUDGE
health check.

Advance the reference every REBASE_RETRIES rejections, unconditionally: a
poisoned reference never looks excessive against itself, so any smarter
condition can stall on the very failure being fixed. Add prevSamples to log
the drift against the preceding sample and the interval against the
reference, which separates a bad pairing from a sustained rate error.

Rationale, sizing of REBASE_RETRIES, TX consequences and field measurements:
doc/wifx/timesync-recovery.md

Signed-off-by: Yannick Serafini <yannick.serafini@wifx.net>
---
